From 5001d8de61f37a8076052e3280f7b71a2711c308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:28:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] m3 particles: partEmit bursts, for emitters and PARC
 copies

A partEmit key owes its value in particles when the playhead steps over
it (WhiteoutFlakes CrossSquirtKeys / SquirtBurst): the sum of the
positive key values crossed since the last update, on top of the rate.
Only animated references (animFlags bit 2) burst; nothing at rest.

- M3SdContainer, M3Stc, M3Stg, M3Skeleton: crossed(animRef, from, to),
  with the loop wrap; summed over every STC of the group with data.
- M3ParticleSystem: frameWindow() tracks the playhead per update; after
  a sequence change the window opens before 0, so a key at 0 fires.
  bursts[] counts burst births per slot.

Known defects:
- Rule ported from WhiteoutFlakes; the in-game look is an operator check.
